Subject: [PATCH] Phase 4 Step 4: Implement SPI0 CMD24 512-byte Read-Modify-Write in driver-SDDVR.s

- Lower COREEND$ from 0xF3FF to 0xF1FF to reserve 512 bytes (0xF200..0xF3FF) for
  the 256-byte RMW sibling buffer (sd_rmw_buf) and sddvr_write_sector while keeping
  the fixed lowcore mailbox at 0xF400 (sddvr_base_lba=0xF408, sddvr_map_lba=0xF428,
  sddvr_map_len=0xF42C) completely unchanged.
- Update DOWRIT in driver-FDCDVR.s (keeping exact 20-byte footprint so dw_offset
  remains at 0x0F78) to preserve DE/HL, compute 16-bit LSN via calcsec, and
  dispatch Local SD writes to sddvr_write_sector.
- Implement full SPI0 CMD17+CMD24 Read-Modify-Write in driver-SDDVR.s with DCT
  write-protect enforcement (bit 7 of DCT+3), Data Response Token validation,
  busy-wait completion, and emulator + real hardware SPI0 compatibility.

--- a/TRSDOS_GLOBAL/equates/equates-versions.s
+++ b/TRSDOS_GLOBAL/equates/equates-versions.s
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
 
 COREMAX$		EQU   	START$+2400h		; Start of application area when no library zone used.
 COREMIN$		EQU   	START$+3000h		; Start of application area with active library area.
-COREEND$		EQU	0F3FFh			; End of usable memory below high driver area (0F400h).
+COREEND$		EQU	0F1FFh			; End of usable memory below high driver area (0F200h).
 
 ENDRAM$			EQU	10000H-1
 
